  "question": {
    "text": "The value of Rydberg constant \\(\\left(R_H\\right)\\) is \\(2.18 \\times 10^{-18} \\mathrm{~J}\\). The velocity of electron having mass \\(9.1 \\times 10^{-31} \\mathrm{~kg}\\) in Bohr's first orbit of hydrogen atom \\(=\\) _______ \\(\\times 10^5 \\mathrm{~ms}^{-1}\\) (nearest integer)."
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "22",
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned} & \\mathrm{V}=2.18 \\times 10^6 \\times \\frac{\\mathrm{Z}}{\\mathrm{n}} \\\\ & =21.8 \\times 10^5 \\times \\frac{1}{1} \\approx 22 \\times 10^5 \\text { (nearest) }\\end{aligned}$"
  }
